  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Madansingh vs Indore Nagar Palika Nigam on 10 March, 2026 Neutral Citation No. 2026:Mphc-Ind:6488 1 In The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh At Indore Before Hon'Ble Shri Justice Gajendra Singh On The 10th Of March, 2026 Criminal Revision No. 619 of 2017 Madansingh Versus Indore Nagar Palika Nigam Appearance: Shri Rajesh Kumar Vyas - Advocate for the petitioner Shri Chinmay, learned counsel for the respondent [R-1 Order",
    "facts": "The proceedings disclosed that at the time of judgment by the appellate Court on 03.05.2017, this revision petitioner was not present and the judgment was passed in his absence and an application under Section 317 of the Cr.P.C., 1973 was preferred by the revision petitioner. This revision petition was preferred on 16.05.2017, but thereafter no one appeared for the petitioner for a long period and vide order dated 06.10.2018, Amicus Currie was appointed to address the Court on behalf of the revision petitioner. 4. As per the order sheet dated 01.08.2024, a report was called from the Superintendent of Jail, Indore and it was intimated that the revision petitioner is not in custody in this case.",
